// Nadia Kowalski (she/her): a midwife at the cottage hospital, mostly night shifts. Practical, tired, very funny.
// Friendship only. Arrives in chapter 2.

=== nadia_intro ===
A woman in scrubs under a raincoat leans on the counter like it's holding her up. # thoughtful
Nadia: Sorry. Night shift. I've been awake since yesterday's yesterday. # happy
Nadia: Nadia. Kowalski. I deliver babies. Not by post. # happy
~ met()
~ note(A midwife at the cottage hospital, mostly on nights.)
-> END

=== nadia_visit ===
Nadia: I came in for one thing and I've forgotten what it was. This happens a lot. # thoughtful
-> END

=== nadia_visit_twins ===
Nadia: Twins last night. Both girls. Both furious about it. # happy
-> END

=== nadia_visit_coffee ===
Nadia: Is it rude to ask if you have a kettle? It's rude. I'm asking anyway. # happy
-> END

=== nadia_visit_2_mara ===
Nadia: I delivered Mara's Poppy, you know. Gorgeous baby. Very loud. Takes after nobody. # happy
~ note(Delivered Mara's daughter, Poppy.)
-> END

=== nadia_request_blanket ===
# fits: plushie_sewn, plushie, scarf
# best: plushie_sewn
Nadia: The maternity ward's teddy box is empty. Every baby goes home with one. # thoughtful
Nadia: Something soft. Something that says somebody made this just for you.
-> END

=== nadia_request_warm ===
# fits: sweater, scarf
# best: sweater
Nadia: The hospital at three in the morning is the coldest place on earth. # neutral
Nadia: I'd like something warm that isn't the regulation cardigan. The regulation cardigan is a crime.
-> END

=== nadia_request_door ===
# fits: hoop_art, sampler
# best: hoop_art
Nadia: My front door needs something. Neighbours keep knocking at the wrong house. # thoughtful
Nadia: Something cheerful with my name on it? Ish? Something that says "the tired one lives here".
-> END

=== nadia_handover_good ===
Nadia: Oh. Oh, that's lovely. I'm not crying, I'm just very tired. # happy
-> END

=== nadia_handover_okay ===
Nadia: Perfect. Honestly. You're a lifesaver. And I'd know. # happy
-> END

=== nadia_handover_poor ===
Nadia: It's... cosy. Cosy is good. I'm a big fan of cosy. # thoughtful
-> END

=== nadia_suggest_yes ===
Nadia: Yes. Make it. Before I fall asleep standing up. # happy
-> END

=== nadia_suggest_buy ===
Nadia: I could knit that on my break. Pattern, please! # happy
-> END

=== nadia_suggest_no ===
Nadia: Not quite me, sorry. Ask me again when I've slept. # thoughtful
-> END

=== nadia_scene_1 ===
Nadia: Can I sit here a minute? Just a minute. # sad
Nadia: Hard night. Everyone's fine. It was just a hard night.
* [Sit as long as you like.]
    You make her tea. She drinks it in silence and leaves a little lighter. # thoughtful
    ~ friendship(10)
* [Do you want to talk about it?]
    Nadia: No. But thank you for asking. Nobody asks. # happy
    ~ friendship(5)
-> END

=== nadia_scene_2 ===
Nadia: I knit on night shift, between babies. I'm terrible at it. # happy
She shows you a scarf with more holes than scarf.
Nadia: It's meant to be lace. It's actually just... mistakes.
~ note(Knits on night shifts, badly and happily.)
* [Let me show you a trick.]
    Twenty minutes later she's stopped dropping stitches. She looks at you like you've invented fire. # surprised
    ~ friendship(10)
* [Mistakes are just lace with confidence.]
    Nadia: I'm putting that on a mug. # happy
    ~ friendship(5)
-> END

=== nadia_scene_3 ===
Nadia: There's a baby on my ward tonight wearing a hat you made. The mother cried. # happy
Nadia: I told her where it came from. You're going to be very busy.
~ friendship(15)
-> END

=== nadia_saturday ===
You and Nadia sleep through most of Saturday in deckchairs on the beach. It's glorious. # happy
Nadia: Best date I've had in years, and I'm not even dating you. # happy
-> END
